WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.690
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.960 --> 00:05.550
The girl from Roopkund is alive.

3
00:09.790 --> 00:13.240
Kyoichi Nanase claimed she was dead.

4
00:13.240 --> 00:15.450
Shiharu is dead.

5
00:15.450 --> 00:19.230
But I don't believe him.

6
00:19.230 --> 00:21.480
You won't look into anything unnecessary?

7
00:21.480 --> 00:24.720
If anything, he seems desperate to hide her.

8
00:26.160 --> 00:29.060
I want nothing to do with this.

9
00:29.060 --> 00:32.070
Please, wait. Shii...

10
00:32.070 --> 00:35.850
The girl from Roopkund needs you!

11
00:35.850 --> 00:39.640
She was already weak the last time I saw her.

12
00:40.650 --> 00:44.880
You're the only person who can save her!

13
01:06.750 --> 01:10.960
Shiharu was an artificially made human being.

14
01:36.520 --> 01:38.210
Haruka.

15
01:47.600 --> 01:50.870
- What are you doing? - Don't you love me?

16
01:50.870 --> 01:52.810
You're acting strange.

17
01:52.810 --> 01:54.990
What do you love about me?

18
01:54.990 --> 01:56.190
Huh?

19
01:56.190 --> 01:58.620
Answer me.

20
01:58.620 --> 02:00.030
I love everything about you.

21
02:00.030 --> 02:01.690
And what's "everything"?

22
02:01.690 --> 02:07.700
Your pretty hair, your beauty, your intelligence - everything.

23
02:08.490 --> 02:14.210
Then you wouldn't love me if I became bald, ugly, and dumb.

24
02:15.500 --> 02:20.250
Well, that wouldn't be you anymore, would it?

25
02:23.490 --> 02:25.080
Yeah.

26
02:26.600 --> 02:28.940
I think so, too.

27
02:28.940 --> 02:30.510
Shiharu?

28
02:31.390 --> 02:33.050
Wait.

29
02:35.320 --> 02:37.230
Shiharu.

30
02:37.230 --> 02:38.750
Shiharu!

31
02:39.950 --> 02:41.270
If something's bothering you, tell me.

32
02:41.270 --> 02:42.210
I already did!

33
02:42.210 --> 02:43.530
I don't understand.

34
02:43.530 --> 02:44.900
That's fine.

35
02:44.900 --> 02:47.380
Don't make things more confusing for me.

36
02:49.300 --> 02:52.080
I don't want you to understand.

37
02:52.080 --> 02:53.970
Does that clear things up?

38
02:57.380 --> 02:59.180
Fine.

39
03:35.960 --> 03:40.850
[The mystery of his sister's life and death] [Despair hidden within the truth]

40
03:40.850 --> 03:42.760
I'm home.

41
03:46.230 --> 03:51.200
[log.7]

42
03:51.200 --> 03:52.960
Shiharu?

43
04:01.110 --> 04:02.680
Shiharu?

44
04:04.520 --> 04:06.100
Aren't you home?

45
04:12.100 --> 04:13.630
Shiharu?

46
04:19.290 --> 04:26.040
So it's been quite some time since she's lost her ability to walk.

47
04:27.240 --> 04:31.240
Could you tell me more about the marks on her skin?

48
04:31.240 --> 04:36.790
The ones I saw were on her hands and neck.

49
04:37.660 --> 04:39.820
I see.

50
04:39.820 --> 04:44.190
The clone's DNA suffered damages after all.

51
04:45.200 --> 04:51.190
But if you're telling the truth,

52
04:51.190 --> 04:55.630
then it's entirely possible she's still alive.

53
04:58.000 --> 05:01.450
Though I suspect she doesn't have long.

54
05:01.450 --> 05:07.640
Nanase and Ishimizaki did well to keep her thriving without me.

55
05:09.110 --> 05:10.830
Dr. Senba.

56
05:10.830 --> 05:14.320
Please ask Mr. Nanase where he's keeping her.

57
05:14.320 --> 05:17.540
- Me? - I know he would tell you.

58
05:17.540 --> 05:20.950
Because you can save her.

59
05:20.950 --> 05:23.500
He would never pass up such an opportunity.

60
05:23.500 --> 05:27.640
My answer is "no".

61
05:28.470 --> 05:32.660
I can't afford to get involved anymore.

62
05:32.660 --> 05:36.020
You aren't worried about her?

63
05:37.180 --> 05:39.750
I am interested. But that's all.

64
05:39.750 --> 05:42.520
You brought her into this world.

65
05:42.520 --> 05:46.590
Your trivial moral reasoning won't change my mind.

66
05:48.660 --> 05:53.100
So you don't think of her as your daughter?

67
05:53.100 --> 05:55.220
My "daughter".

68
05:57.750 --> 06:02.170
A child I knew nothing about for 30 years, my "daughter".

69
06:03.060 --> 06:06.520
They ought to realize their selfish desires

70
06:06.520 --> 06:13.020
ruined any potential for scientific advancements.

71
06:13.020 --> 06:16.220
Nanase is especially guilty in that regard.

72
06:16.220 --> 06:19.000
- I just... - Quiet.

73
06:19.000 --> 06:22.510
Their actions have brought very real consequences to my life.

74
06:22.510 --> 06:25.940
I just want her be alive.

75
06:28.020 --> 06:30.310
I called my security on you.

76
06:30.310 --> 06:33.170
Feel free to stay if you want to be arrested.

77
06:33.170 --> 06:38.010
I can't be entertaining this any longer.

78
06:55.190 --> 06:57.070
What are you doing here?

79
06:57.070 --> 06:59.110
Sir.

80
06:59.110 --> 07:02.150
Isn't there something you've been hiding from me?

81
07:03.110 --> 07:04.950
What are you referring to?

82
07:05.960 --> 07:09.040
As I was looking into our finances,

83
07:09.040 --> 07:15.180
I noticed some funds related to "log.0" were still being utilized.

84
07:15.770 --> 07:20.410
They were deftly hidden through distributions to a shell corporation.

85
07:24.240 --> 07:27.200
Sir, did you think I wouldn't notice?

86
07:28.400 --> 07:31.530
You taught me to be thorough.

87
07:31.530 --> 07:33.800
What is the money being used for?

88
07:34.700 --> 07:37.890
Order me to keep it under wraps, and I will.

89
07:37.890 --> 07:40.480
But must I be kept in the dark as well?

90
07:44.860 --> 07:46.700
Please, tell me the truth.

91
07:47.730 --> 07:50.230
Is "log.0" still active?

92
07:54.850 --> 07:56.810
I wouldn't know.

93
08:20.020 --> 08:24.050
Morning. Did you get it?

94
08:24.050 --> 08:27.120
Yes. Everything pertaining to Roopkund.

95
08:27.120 --> 08:29.130
Score.

96
08:29.130 --> 08:31.630
Want a drink to celebrate?

97
08:31.630 --> 08:35.200
Maybe it's too early for that.

98
08:38.350 --> 08:41.660
Take a seat wherever.

99
08:41.660 --> 08:44.030
I run this bar.

100
08:44.030 --> 08:45.780
Just kidding.

101
08:45.780 --> 08:50.410
I rented the place so we'd get some privacy.

102
08:50.410 --> 08:56.230
Honestly, I drank till morning 'cause I didn't want to go home.

103
09:00.230 --> 09:06.420
Was too scared to find myself alone and all.

104
09:07.870 --> 09:14.000
Some crazy truth we got ourselves, huh?

105
09:16.410 --> 09:20.530
Do you believe them? It sounds ridiculous to me.

106
09:20.530 --> 09:28.100
I'm more convinced, knowing Kayoko Senba is involved.

107
09:30.080 --> 09:31.410
Excuse me.

108
09:31.410 --> 09:32.870
- Sir. - Yes?

109
09:32.870 --> 09:34.960
You won't release our names, right?

110
09:34.960 --> 09:38.980
No, of course not. I promise.

111
09:41.280 --> 09:45.900
I only ask because of the rumors. Not like I believe them, but...

112
09:45.900 --> 09:47.370
Rumors?

113
09:48.050 --> 09:51.480
They say those who bring trouble to Plantae

114
09:51.480 --> 09:55.550
are punished by the spirit of the Holy One.

115
09:58.770 --> 10:01.770
I assume my fellow journalist, Onodera,

116
10:01.770 --> 10:07.170
was murdered by this "spirit" of theirs.

117
10:08.230 --> 10:10.660
All that's left is his bones, and nothing else.

118
10:24.500 --> 10:26.720
That man, Ushio.

119
10:27.900 --> 10:31.080
Is he acting on Plantae's orders?

120
10:31.080 --> 10:33.340
Who else would boss him around?

121
10:34.850 --> 10:37.050
Kyoichi Nanase.

122
10:38.230 --> 10:42.070
Their interests do align.

123
10:42.070 --> 10:46.000
But I'm more inclined to believe this is all Plantae.

124
10:49.700 --> 10:52.470
The biggest surprise here,

125
10:53.830 --> 10:57.460
is that they went and created a person.

126
10:57.460 --> 11:01.150
No country in the world would legalize human clones.

127
11:01.150 --> 11:04.190
But the technology in creating one holds great value.

128
11:04.190 --> 11:06.750
Medical advancements would surge forth.

129
11:10.230 --> 11:12.580
Find evidence of this clone at once.

130
11:12.580 --> 11:15.200
We'll contact the main branch in China afterwards.

131
11:16.650 --> 11:18.100
Yes, sir.

132
11:25.690 --> 11:28.410
I've checked its contents.

133
11:28.410 --> 11:32.790
Everything pertains to the making of a clone.

134
11:37.630 --> 11:40.210
So it's all true.

135
11:40.210 --> 11:44.650
There really was an artificial human

136
11:44.650 --> 11:48.290
walking among us.

137
11:50.290 --> 11:53.000
Sends shivers down my spine, I tell you.

138
11:54.620 --> 12:00.950
I bet Onodera felt the same way.

139
12:04.400 --> 12:07.570
We can't help it.

140
12:07.570 --> 12:10.040
It's what makes us journalists.

141
12:11.450 --> 12:15.390
I'll be sure his findings see a proper conclusion.

142
12:17.780 --> 12:20.050
I don't want you to write about this.

143
12:20.920 --> 12:23.460
My sister's existence will be known to the world.

144
12:25.320 --> 12:27.400
Don't worry.

145
12:27.400 --> 12:32.460
I won't be hasty about publishing our evidence.

146
12:34.040 --> 12:36.060
I'll hold onto the data.

147
12:36.060 --> 12:38.670
It'll be useful as a bargaining chip to find my sister.

148
12:38.670 --> 12:41.330
I promise not to put you in a bind.

149
12:41.330 --> 12:44.210
Publishing an article will do that anyway.

150
12:44.210 --> 12:47.560
Numerous people have died over this.

151
12:47.560 --> 12:51.200
Leave it be, and more will follow.

152
12:52.690 --> 12:55.190
You plan to publish the article immediately.

153
12:57.030 --> 13:02.150
These people are killing folks left and right

154
13:02.150 --> 13:05.810
all to keep this girl under wraps.

155
13:05.810 --> 13:07.200
The public deserves to know.

156
13:07.200 --> 13:09.580
Then what happens to my sister?

157
13:12.850 --> 13:15.140
"Punished by the spirit of the Holy One".

158
13:17.040 --> 13:18.840
Hear what I'm getting at?

159
13:20.580 --> 13:22.740
What do you mean?

160
13:22.740 --> 13:25.180
The "Holy One" they're so scared of,

161
13:26.150 --> 13:30.390
is your sister, the Holy Woman.

162
13:32.620 --> 13:34.790
What sort of assumption is that?

163
13:34.790 --> 13:37.020
I won't beat around the bush.

164
13:37.020 --> 13:42.100
I suspect your younger sister is the one behind all this.

165
13:44.870 --> 13:46.160
What?

166
13:46.920 --> 13:48.480
Why Shiharu?

167
13:48.480 --> 13:52.020
She wants to protect herself.

168
13:52.020 --> 13:54.790
Your sister is the Holy Woman.

169
13:54.790 --> 13:58.390
If anyone could control Ushio, it'd be her.

170
13:58.930 --> 14:03.020
And your father.

171
14:03.020 --> 14:06.240
He was all in on helping Plantae

172
14:06.240 --> 14:09.220
create a clone.

173
14:09.820 --> 14:14.010
It wouldn't surprise me if he obeys the Holy Woman, too.

174
14:15.740 --> 14:17.570
- Give me that! - Hey!

175
14:17.570 --> 14:19.380
Think about it!

176
14:19.380 --> 14:21.750
Shiharu Nanase is an artificial human being!

177
14:21.750 --> 14:25.040
Can you really call a thing like her your sister?

178
14:25.040 --> 14:26.890
Let go!

179
14:36.360 --> 14:38.050
[Yui Ishimizaki]

180
14:40.110 --> 14:41.730
[Yui Ishimizaki]

181
14:41.730 --> 14:45.660
[Kyoichi told me everything about Shiharu]

182
14:49.990 --> 14:52.510
[Senba]

183
14:53.670 --> 14:56.550
Damn it, why isn't anyone answering?

184
14:56.550 --> 15:00.700
Tomoe is a stay-at-home mother. I assumed she would be around.

185
15:00.700 --> 15:02.750
Guess we'll wait.

186
15:02.750 --> 15:06.330
We can't stay long. We're ignoring orders to be here.

187
15:06.330 --> 15:10.720
Still a bootlicker for headquarters?

188
15:12.570 --> 15:13.950
Tada.

189
15:13.950 --> 15:15.810
Damn it!

190
15:41.140 --> 15:47.090
I thought you'd feel more comfortable meeting where there's a crowd.

191
15:49.050 --> 15:52.580
- Want a croquette? - What did he tell you about Shiharu?

192
15:57.370 --> 15:59.080
Everything.

193
16:00.190 --> 16:04.880
Roopkund, the process... Everything.

194
16:04.880 --> 16:07.120
Where is Shiharu?

195
16:08.920 --> 16:13.600
Kyoichi said she had passed away.

196
16:14.330 --> 16:17.120
- But I think she's alive! - Who are you?

197
16:20.650 --> 16:22.470
Answer me.

198
16:28.120 --> 16:32.550
I'm Ishimizaki's daughter, Mari.

199
16:35.620 --> 16:37.150
What?

200
16:37.150 --> 16:40.840
I met Mari. She was in a wheelchair.

201
16:40.840 --> 16:43.130
The Professor called that girl his daughter.

202
16:43.130 --> 16:47.190
My father lied to you.

203
16:47.190 --> 16:49.000
He had no choice.

204
16:49.000 --> 16:50.870
Why?

205
16:50.870 --> 16:53.620
Why did he have to lie?

206
16:58.160 --> 17:03.020
Who were you looking for all this time?

207
17:23.980 --> 17:27.430
The Professor brought that girl in, on the day of a heavy storm?

208
17:28.210 --> 17:31.550
Right.

209
17:32.910 --> 17:35.860
But you can't tell me who this girl is.

210
17:41.330 --> 17:42.830
Why?

211
17:45.080 --> 17:49.020
Because I promised her I wouldn't.

212
17:49.990 --> 17:52.060
What's the point of a promise like that?

213
18:18.520 --> 18:20.550
I'm not hiding anything else from you.

214
18:21.740 --> 18:26.190
I know I'm asking the impossible, but I want you to trust me.

215
18:26.190 --> 18:30.220
Haruka, I promise you and I share a goal.

216
18:37.310 --> 18:38.850
Alright.

217
18:47.570 --> 18:52.170
I'm sorry about your father. That must have been difficult.

218
18:56.940 --> 19:02.060
He was one of the few individuals who truly understood me.

219
19:06.330 --> 19:12.810
He'd always entertain my thoughts, too.

220
19:12.810 --> 19:15.550
I could tell him anything.

221
19:17.740 --> 19:22.680
But in these last few years, he changed.

222
19:28.310 --> 19:32.800
The last time I saw him

223
19:33.920 --> 19:40.620
was another day I couldn't ask about his secrets.

224
19:47.080 --> 19:48.970
Didn't notice you there.

225
19:50.160 --> 19:52.090
How's Shii?

226
19:52.090 --> 19:54.530
She's sleeping right now.

227
19:54.530 --> 19:56.410
Let her rest.

228
19:57.270 --> 19:59.520
Shiharu is okay.

229
19:59.520 --> 20:01.590
I promise.

230
20:04.620 --> 20:06.410
Okay.

231
20:11.270 --> 20:15.220
Dad. Have you been eating?

232
20:17.150 --> 20:18.430
Huh?

233
20:19.250 --> 20:21.540
Oh, yes. I have.

234
20:23.510 --> 20:25.730
Let me whip up something for you.

235
20:29.450 --> 20:31.890
What?

236
20:34.160 --> 20:36.010
Mari...

237
20:36.660 --> 20:38.830
I don't need to worry about you anymore.

238
20:39.830 --> 20:47.150
Everyone will come to love your endearing attitude.

239
20:48.770 --> 20:51.200
Stop it, you're embarrassing me.

240
20:53.120 --> 20:55.450
Never change, Mari.

241
20:57.500 --> 20:59.210
I won't.

242
20:59.210 --> 21:05.400
My father was prepared to confess about Roopkund.

243
21:07.030 --> 21:09.090
I regret not asking.

244
21:10.160 --> 21:14.790
I should have pestered him more.

245
21:15.570 --> 21:18.750
Maybe something would have changed.

246
21:20.590 --> 21:25.470
That regret is why I'm so determined now.

247
21:31.080 --> 21:33.020
It'll be okay, Haruka.

248
21:34.230 --> 21:40.080
We will find Shiharu. I promise.

249
21:49.150 --> 21:52.170
What if...

250
21:54.690 --> 21:58.370
What if we find Shiharu, and she's changed?

251
21:59.780 --> 22:01.830
What do you mean?

252
22:02.520 --> 22:08.620
Someone suspects Shiharu is the one behind all these incidents.

253
22:09.210 --> 22:11.400
That's impossible.

254
22:11.400 --> 22:13.420
It's really not.

255
22:13.420 --> 22:19.040
Anyone who suspects her is a fool.

256
22:22.190 --> 22:23.710
Yeah.

257
22:26.540 --> 22:28.140
They're a fool.

258
22:31.790 --> 22:33.090
I don't understand.

259
22:33.090 --> 22:37.690
Like I said, I didn't get the evidence.

260
22:37.690 --> 22:40.780
I'll try again from another angle.

261
22:40.780 --> 22:45.150
Kayoko Senba seems like my best bet.

262
22:45.150 --> 22:47.770
What happened to Haruka Nanase?

263
22:47.770 --> 22:49.600
He gave me nothing to work with.

264
22:50.690 --> 22:52.610
I'll change his mind.

265
22:52.610 --> 22:54.860
Tell me how to reach him.

266
22:54.860 --> 22:58.200
That's not my information to give.

267
22:58.200 --> 23:01.490
- I know it's written in there. - Hey, no touching.

268
23:01.490 --> 23:03.950
This is a journalist's soul.

269
23:08.520 --> 23:10.180
Kayoko Senba, you said?

270
23:10.180 --> 23:14.580
That's right. Let's forget Haruka Nanase.

271
23:19.760 --> 23:22.280
I'm so sorry.

272
23:22.280 --> 23:24.230
I only have instant foods.

273
23:24.230 --> 23:28.620
But you should definitely eat something.

274
23:30.410 --> 23:32.390
I'll heat up the croquettes.

275
23:34.930 --> 23:37.360
Right, I should boil the water first.

276
23:37.360 --> 23:40.470
Here, I'll do it.

277
23:41.580 --> 23:43.640
Thank you.

278
23:55.410 --> 23:57.020
Haruka.

279
23:58.110 --> 24:02.510
Could you tell me more about Shiharu?

280
24:02.510 --> 24:04.250
Huh?

281
24:04.250 --> 24:06.830
You told me stories about her before.

282
24:09.080 --> 24:11.120
Please?

283
24:18.150 --> 24:20.720
She once said she wanted a part-time job.

284
24:22.740 --> 24:28.560
What I considered a pain, was a source of wonder to her.

285
24:29.350 --> 24:31.580
What're you doing?

286
24:31.580 --> 24:33.200
Welcome home.

287
24:33.200 --> 24:35.380
I just finished reading.

288
24:35.380 --> 24:37.180
Then let's go to the gallery.

289
24:37.910 --> 24:40.520
Haruka, you don't work part-time?

290
24:40.520 --> 24:42.290
No, why?

291
24:42.290 --> 24:44.080
It seems fun.

292
24:44.080 --> 24:49.110
"Manager, that's not what the manual says."

293
24:49.110 --> 24:50.820
Huh? What manager?

294
24:50.820 --> 24:53.370
I just wanted to try saying it.

295
24:53.370 --> 24:56.910
"That's not my mistake."

296
24:56.910 --> 25:00.270
"I meant to come in, really."

297
25:00.270 --> 25:02.000
Is that for when you skip work?

298
25:02.000 --> 25:03.620
I don't know.

299
25:04.510 --> 25:08.630
I wouldn't know.

300
25:15.360 --> 25:17.390
Work is more trouble than it's worth.

301
25:18.620 --> 25:23.900
Then how's this? "Hasegawa, we share a shift on Christmas."

302
25:23.900 --> 25:25.850
Who the heck is Hasegawa?

303
25:25.850 --> 25:28.520
"No venting allowed, Haruka."

304
25:28.520 --> 25:30.380
I'm employed with you?

305
25:35.210 --> 25:38.250
I usually started our conversations.

306
25:38.250 --> 25:42.840
Shiharu would be too absorbed in a book.

307
25:58.630 --> 26:01.020
Thank you.

308
26:01.810 --> 26:04.060
For telling me about her.

309
27:00.440 --> 27:02.510
It's no use.

310
27:02.510 --> 27:05.690
I could contact Kayoko Senba's son,

311
27:05.690 --> 27:11.110
but he said his mother left for a vacation.

312
27:11.110 --> 27:13.040
I see.

313
27:14.080 --> 27:15.760
What're you up to?

314
27:16.490 --> 27:20.010
I figured I'd stop being a corporate bootlicker.

315
27:40.230 --> 27:42.400
The police contacted you?

316
27:42.400 --> 27:45.930
No. Don't tell a soul I'm here.

317
27:48.210 --> 27:51.000
I'll be fine.

318
27:51.650 --> 27:55.180
You take care as well, alright?

319
28:03.490 --> 28:09.210
Sir, the elevator is for guests only.

320
28:10.340 --> 28:13.540
May I ask for your room key?

321
28:15.730 --> 28:18.560
Has Tomoe contacted you?

322
28:19.820 --> 28:23.790
What is that woman doing?

323
28:26.570 --> 28:31.450
I hope you've been feeding Keita well.

324
28:35.190 --> 28:37.060
Room service is here.

325
28:37.060 --> 28:39.220
I'll stay in touch.

326
28:52.440 --> 28:55.190
I've brought your water.

327
28:55.190 --> 28:56.980
Would you leave it inside?

328
28:56.980 --> 29:00.020
Of course.

329
29:24.330 --> 29:26.940
[Mikio Maehara]

330
29:39.460 --> 29:42.900
[Tsuyoshi Kojima] [Xin Ming Ah Japan Representative]

331
29:42.900 --> 29:46.420
[Dear Haruka Nanase, I believe we can assist you...]

332
30:12.520 --> 30:15.500
Haruka! Where are you going?

333
30:15.500 --> 30:19.290
To meet someone. I'll be fine alone.

334
30:19.290 --> 30:20.920
Wait.

335
30:20.920 --> 30:26.220
"Do all that you can today, to see further progress tomorrow."

336
30:26.910 --> 30:30.460
I know that one. Isaac Newton.

337
30:32.400 --> 30:36.010
Not bad.

338
30:55.690 --> 30:58.060
You really came alone.

339
31:02.690 --> 31:04.940
I wouldn't disobey the President's son.

340
31:04.940 --> 31:07.040
Without telling my father?

341
31:11.370 --> 31:14.280
What did you need to ask me?

342
31:14.280 --> 31:16.210
Or is this about your father?

343
31:16.210 --> 31:18.640
Tell me where Shiharu is.

344
31:20.150 --> 31:21.590
Her again.

345
31:21.590 --> 31:24.580
I have the all the findings from Roopkund.

346
31:26.480 --> 31:28.410
What are you referring to?

347
31:29.280 --> 31:32.810
The research you people are so desperate to hide.

348
31:36.900 --> 31:39.500
Show me, and maybe it'll ring a bell.

349
31:44.160 --> 31:49.810
Creating Shiharu from the bones of Roopkund. Does that help?

350
32:02.350 --> 32:04.040
Please.

351
32:05.130 --> 32:06.970
Tell me where she is.

352
32:08.520 --> 32:10.890
Where is Shiharu?

353
32:13.990 --> 32:15.800
Create?

354
32:17.040 --> 32:19.580
You say we "created" your sister?

355
32:29.160 --> 32:31.130
Drop the act, now.

356
32:34.030 --> 32:37.680
That girl only exists in your mind.

357
32:39.780 --> 32:41.520
Are you like Kayoko Senba?

358
32:43.370 --> 32:48.680
Were you also told the cloning was a failure?

359
32:50.840 --> 32:53.650
No, I won't believe that.

360
32:54.770 --> 32:56.850
Because you people...

361
32:57.910 --> 33:01.850
You people murdered Professor Ishimizaki to keep Shiharu a secret!

362
33:01.850 --> 33:05.250
- What? - And he's not the only one you've killed!

363
33:08.710 --> 33:12.750
I see.

364
33:12.750 --> 33:15.150
I get it now.

365
33:15.150 --> 33:20.490
Your search has brought plenty of others misfortune.

366
33:20.490 --> 33:23.020
Kyoichi Nanase's the one giving orders.

367
33:23.020 --> 33:27.950
He just wants to keep his company afloat!

368
33:30.230 --> 33:32.590
I can't be entertaining your delusions.

369
33:32.590 --> 33:36.000
You're his right-hand man. I know you know everything!

370
33:44.630 --> 33:46.680
What?

371
33:49.670 --> 33:52.250
I don't know anything.

372
33:54.480 --> 33:56.720
Not a damn thing.

373
34:17.730 --> 34:19.460
Mari.

374
34:23.400 --> 34:27.830
Is this about...

375
34:29.540 --> 34:34.120
I'm sorry. We haven't made much progress in regards to your father's case.

376
34:34.120 --> 34:36.150
I see.

377
34:36.150 --> 34:39.740
But this case is strange, in many ways.

378
34:39.740 --> 34:43.000
So I had something I wanted to ask.

379
34:43.790 --> 34:45.440
Alright.

380
34:45.440 --> 34:49.150
When Nanase was attacked by the man named Ushio,

381
34:49.150 --> 34:54.060
he claimed he was accompanied by Professor Ishimizaki's niece.

382
34:54.060 --> 34:57.660
But that was you, wasn't it?

383
34:59.580 --> 35:03.130
Well, I...

384
35:03.130 --> 35:06.610
I'm not trying to interrogate you about that.

385
35:06.610 --> 35:08.810
Let me rephrase my question.

386
35:08.810 --> 35:14.600
You were helping Nanase search for his sister, correct?

387
35:19.310 --> 35:25.200
Except, this sister of his doesn't exist on paper.

388
35:30.450 --> 35:33.550
I want to start by searching for this person.

389
35:35.310 --> 35:36.750
What?

390
35:39.620 --> 35:46.620
This time, I want to try believing in Haruka Nanase.

391
35:48.020 --> 35:53.640
Is there anything you know about Shiharu Nanase?

392
36:00.230 --> 36:04.520
People who have no citizenship each have their own reasons.

393
36:04.520 --> 36:09.040
If Shiharu is in a similar situation, we must find her right away.

394
36:09.040 --> 36:10.400
As it stands now,

395
36:10.400 --> 36:14.040
she's unable to receive legal medical attention should she need it.

396
36:22.020 --> 36:28.210
Shiharu Nanase exists somewhere, doesn't she?

397
36:35.120 --> 36:38.080
Reach out again when you're ready to talk.

398
36:38.080 --> 36:43.140
I mostly wanted to break the ice today.

399
36:55.480 --> 36:58.650
Haruka. Where are you?

400
36:58.650 --> 37:01.020
Is Shiharu dead?

401
37:02.480 --> 37:05.050
You must've heard from Ishimizaki's daughter.

402
37:08.460 --> 37:11.210
How can you act so nonchalant?

403
37:12.540 --> 37:14.010
You...

404
37:15.560 --> 37:18.840
Do you realize what you've done?

405
37:19.780 --> 37:21.650
Of course.

406
37:28.570 --> 37:30.660
Did you...

407
37:34.390 --> 37:36.290
Did you kill Shiharu?

408
37:39.320 --> 37:44.310
You used my mother to create a clone.

409
37:44.310 --> 37:47.180
Isn't that why she died?

410
37:48.450 --> 37:50.800
Who told you that?

411
37:51.660 --> 37:53.500
Kayoko Senba.

412
37:54.380 --> 37:57.220
I have all the files on Roopkund as well.

413
37:58.330 --> 38:01.580
What sort of stunts did you pull?

414
38:01.580 --> 38:04.050
I haven't caused anyone trouble.

415
38:05.610 --> 38:07.410
At least, not yet.

416
38:11.620 --> 38:13.130
Haruka.

417
38:14.520 --> 38:16.540
Shiharu is alive.

418
38:17.470 --> 38:21.620
Shiharu is very much alive.

419
38:21.620 --> 38:26.840
You must realize the information you have is a burden to her.

420
38:28.350 --> 38:30.120
Why?

421
38:32.580 --> 38:35.750
Why are you doing all this?

422
38:36.770 --> 38:38.920
Everything I do is for Shiharu's sake.

423
38:41.660 --> 38:43.800
Where is she?

424
38:47.410 --> 38:50.160
Where the hell is Shiharu?

425
38:53.080 --> 38:56.410
Let's talk in person. Alone.

426
38:57.960 --> 38:59.980
Trust me.

427
39:00.950 --> 39:03.710
You have no other choice.

428
39:15.950 --> 39:19.210
"No venting allowed, Haruka."

429
39:43.520 --> 39:46.750
I'm glad you've come.

430
39:49.460 --> 39:50.910
Follow me.

431
39:52.270 --> 39:56.520
You've made a sound decision, Haruka Nanase.

432
39:56.520 --> 39:58.520
You said you'd help, but how?

433
39:58.520 --> 40:00.960
Please, have a seat.

434
40:04.460 --> 40:10.850
I hear you suspect your step-father and head of Nichie Pharmaceutical,

435
40:10.850 --> 40:16.890
Kyoichi Nanase, of a number of things.

436
40:16.890 --> 40:19.700
What bothers you most? The thing with your mother?

437
40:19.700 --> 40:22.320
Or your missing sister?

438
40:22.320 --> 40:25.100
I see Hirama has told you of my situation.

439
40:26.310 --> 40:32.770
I will admit. We have done our own investigating as well.

440
40:32.770 --> 40:38.410
As such, I believe our goals are aligned with one another.

441
40:39.060 --> 40:40.540
How so?

442
40:40.540 --> 40:45.380
If Nichie goes under, it becomes easier for both of us to take action.

443
40:48.020 --> 40:51.520
Nichie Pharmaceutical - or rather, Kyoichi Nanase,

444
40:51.520 --> 40:57.650
who has dabbled in cloning tech, is now Plantae's loyal dog.

445
40:57.650 --> 41:00.150
Let me cut to the chase.

446
41:06.150 --> 41:10.800
Please think of this money as our way of aiding your search.

447
41:12.870 --> 41:14.970
What is it you want from me?

448
41:18.030 --> 41:22.010
You have the data on Roopkund, yes?

449
41:24.780 --> 41:26.280
I had a feeling.

450
41:26.280 --> 41:30.600
Our hope is for Nichie to be officially prosecuted.

451
41:30.600 --> 41:31.870
Furthermore,

452
41:31.870 --> 41:36.200
we plan to re-establish the company as a trustworthy corporation.

453
41:36.200 --> 41:39.900
Though human cloning is illegal,

454
41:39.900 --> 41:43.720
the technology behind it can be used for medical advancements.

455
41:44.790 --> 41:47.430
I was a fool for expecting anything from you.

456
41:53.280 --> 41:56.000
Negotiations haven't ended yet.

457
41:58.210 --> 42:00.690
Think about it.

458
42:00.690 --> 42:05.310
The circumstances surrounding Shiharu grow unruly by the day.

459
42:05.310 --> 42:09.190
Surely, you cannot protect her alone.

460
42:10.100 --> 42:14.850
I suspect your younger sister is the one behind all this.

461
42:15.500 --> 42:19.660
We will hold onto the data, for your own safety as well.

462
42:32.120 --> 42:34.650
A wise choice indeed.

463
42:40.400 --> 42:43.260
Don't ever bother me again.

464
42:43.920 --> 42:45.590
You're in my way.

465
42:45.590 --> 42:47.720
Bastard...

466
42:48.310 --> 42:54.380
If I don't report back to Hirama, he will call the police on you.

467
43:02.940 --> 43:05.910
It seems there's been a misunderstanding.

468
43:05.910 --> 43:08.320
I only wished to talk business with you.

469
43:08.320 --> 43:10.390
Well, I'm not interested.

470
43:11.120 --> 43:14.710
Then please, make your way out.

471
43:24.200 --> 43:25.660
You alright?

472
43:25.660 --> 43:27.730
Barely.

473
43:27.730 --> 43:30.880
So? Did you get anything good out of them?

474
43:30.880 --> 43:32.470
No.

475
43:32.470 --> 43:34.220
Figures.

476
43:36.750 --> 43:38.960
Sorry about my accusations yesterday.

477
43:39.730 --> 43:43.100
So, what's your next move?

478
43:44.120 --> 43:45.920
The same as it's always been.

479
43:47.240 --> 43:49.660
Find my sister.

480
44:01.270 --> 44:04.330
Shii, could you give this a taste?

481
44:04.330 --> 44:05.870
Sure.

482
44:11.200 --> 44:13.250
That tastes wrong.

483
44:16.550 --> 44:18.840
It's good enough.

484
44:18.840 --> 44:19.910
It's not.

485
44:19.910 --> 44:25.730
"Do all that you can today, to see further progress tomorrow."

486
44:25.730 --> 44:28.150
I know that one.

487
44:28.150 --> 44:30.350
- Isaac Newton! - Isaac Newton!

488
44:48.060 --> 44:49.520
Hello?

489
44:49.520 --> 44:54.710
Please help me find Shiharu Nanase.

490
45:00.610 --> 45:01.980
Hello?

491
45:04.810 --> 45:06.860
A package, for me?

492
45:47.270 --> 45:50.490
[Keita]

493
45:51.320 --> 45:53.280
[Keita]
